===Etymology===
{{compound|en|spoon|feed}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈspunˌfid/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈspuːnfiːd/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|spoon|feed}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[spoon]]-[[feed]]|spoon-feeds|spoon-feeding|spoon-fed}}

# To help somebody (usually a [[baby]] or elder) to [[eat]] using a [[spoon]]; to feed using a spoon.
# To overly [[pamper]] or indulge someone, so that they do not act or think for themselves.
#: {{uxi|en|I can help you with your homework, but you must understand the concept, because I will not '''spoon-feed''' you.}}
# To give in an overly pampering way, so that they do not act or think for themselves.
#: {{uxi|en|What do you mean "I don't know"? I'm practically '''spoon-feeding''' you the answer!}}
# To [[explain]] in [[simple]] words; to explain [[in words of one syllable]]; to [[spell out]].

